---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who this prediction markets guide is for, what we cover, and how we stay independent."
	pubDate={new Date('June 4 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		This site is for anyone curious about prediction markets — whether you have never placed a trade
		or you are comparing platforms before signing up. You do not need a finance background or crypto
		experience to follow along. We explain concepts in plain English and focus on what actually matters
		when you choose where to trade.
	</p>

	<p>
		Here you will find beginner-friendly guides on how prediction markets work, plus honest
		comparisons of major platforms including Kalshi, Polymarket, and Crypto.com. We cover who each
		platform suits, how they differ on regulation and access, and what to check before you create an
		account. The goal is to help you make an informed choice, not to hype any single option.
	</p>

	<p>
		This is an independent, educational resource. We are not a broker, exchange, or financial
		adviser, and we do not speak for Kalshi, Polymarket, Crypto.com, or any other company. Guides and
		comparisons are written to be useful and accurate; when we link to platforms, we explain how that
		relationship works on our <a href="/how-we-make-money">How we make money</a> page. Nothing here is
		personalized investment advice — always do your own research and only risk what you can afford to
		lose.
	</p>
</Layout>
